WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.474 --> 00:00:16.882
Zann woke up the next morning to the sound of a bird singing outside the window.

2
00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:20.744
For a second he thought he was back in Swamp Bottom.

3
00:00:21.245 --> 00:00:25.167
The bird's song sounded a lot like one he'd heard most mornings there.

4
00:00:26.148 --> 00:00:28.390
But when he opened his eyes, he sighed.

5
00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:31.612
"I'm still in Terrica," he thought.

6
00:00:32.404 --> 00:00:37.047
He sat up and looked out the window, but the bird was hidden in a lush tree outside.

7
00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:42.111
"I guess birds are similar in every world," he said with a yawn.

8
00:00:43.311 --> 00:00:44.572
The room was empty.

9
00:00:45.573 --> 00:00:48.595
Zann dressed quickly and then headed out to the main room.

10
00:00:49.135 --> 00:00:51.877
He found Perda and Mellis eating breakfast at the table.

11
00:00:52.637 --> 00:00:54.939
"Here's something you might like," Perda was saying.

12
00:00:55.339 --> 00:00:58.942
She snapped her fingers, and a platter of puckerberry pancakes appeared.

13
00:00:59.722 --> 00:01:00.743
Mellis took a bite.

14
00:01:00.763 --> 00:01:02.908
"Wow!" she said.

15
00:01:02.928 --> 00:01:05.530
"These taste a lot better than porridge."

16
00:01:06.991 --> 00:01:08.772
Zann joined the girls at the table.

17
00:01:08.792 --> 00:01:12.894
"After breakfast, we'll give you a few more magic lessons," he said.

18
00:01:12.914 --> 00:01:15.275
"Then Perda and I can head to the wormhole."

19
00:01:16.056 --> 00:01:17.877
Mellis took another bite of the pancakes.

20
00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:22.179
"My friend Anso from the village loves sweet things," she said.

21
00:01:22.199 --> 00:01:25.381
"Will you teach him to make some of these foods before you leave?"

22
00:01:25.401 --> 00:01:27.402
"Sure," Perda said.

23
00:01:27.422 --> 00:01:30.044
"We'll zap to the village after we finish eating.

24
00:01:30.712 --> 00:01:33.533
We'll teach you and your friends everything you want to know."

25
00:01:33.553 --> 00:01:36.215
"No, you won't."

26
00:01:37.115 --> 00:01:40.196
Vilkor strode into the room just in time to hear her.

27
00:01:40.857 --> 00:01:42.438
Zira was right behind him.

28
00:01:42.458 --> 00:01:46.720
"We don't want you to tell anyone about magic."

29
00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.702
"What?" Zann traded a confused look with Perda and Mellis.

30
00:01:51.722 --> 00:01:54.003
"It's not like magic is a secret.

31
00:01:54.523 --> 00:01:56.104
Everybody can see that things are changing."

32
00:01:56.724 --> 00:02:01.588
"They see only that plants are growing and there's more water around," Zira said.

33
00:02:01.608 --> 00:02:03.310
"They don't know why.

34
00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:04.791
And it's better that way."

35
00:02:04.811 --> 00:02:06.632
"What do you mean?"

36
00:02:07.073 --> 00:02:07.713
Zann asked.

37
00:02:08.354 --> 00:02:09.775
Vilkor's eyes gleamed.

38
00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:13.198
"Who knows what would happen if everyone could use magic?"

39
00:02:13.558 --> 00:02:13.918
he said.

40
00:02:13.938 --> 00:02:17.942
"It's better for everyone if Zira and I are in charge.

41
00:02:19.022 --> 00:02:22.886
We can provide magical services for anyone who needs them."

42
00:02:24.047 --> 00:02:25.448
"Right," Zira said.

43
00:02:26.068 --> 00:02:31.491
"It's safer if only Vilkor and I and perhaps a few additional people—" "What?"

44
00:02:32.312 --> 00:02:33.452
Vilkor glanced at her.

45
00:02:34.213 --> 00:02:36.734
"We didn't talk about including anyone else."

46
00:02:38.275 --> 00:02:39.596
Zira patted his arm.

47
00:02:40.596 --> 00:02:41.297
"Not yet.

48
00:02:41.957 --> 00:02:46.320
First, we need to determine how far this magic energy has spread from the well.

49
00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:54.420
If it has reached beyond our village, we'll need local deputies in other villages to help control—er, I

50
00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.281
mean, manage things."

51
00:02:56.301 --> 00:02:59.642
"That's not fair," Perda said with a frown.

52
00:02:59.662 --> 00:03:02.003
"Magic should be for everyone.

53
00:03:02.563 --> 00:03:05.365
Besides, people will figure it out on their own soon enough."

54
00:03:06.325 --> 00:03:08.886
Zira narrowed her eyes at Zann and Perda.

55
00:03:08.906 --> 00:03:13.408
"Weren't you visitors talking about going back to your own world?"

56
00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:17.209
Vilkor laughed.

57
00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:22.992
"Stop humoring them with this silly talk of other worlds."

58
00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:29.210
"Well, wherever they came from, I think they should return there soon," Zira said.

59
00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.730
"Or what?"

60
00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:31.930
Perda demanded.

61
00:03:32.531 --> 00:03:33.431
Vilkor frowned.

62
00:03:33.451 --> 00:03:37.032
"How dare you speak so insolently, girl!"

63
00:03:38.072 --> 00:03:42.613
Zira didn't say a word to Perda, but Zann saw her gray eyes grow narrow.

64
00:03:43.314 --> 00:03:45.074
A second later Perda gasped.

65
00:03:45.194 --> 00:03:47.555
"Let's get out of here," Perda said.

66
00:03:48.115 --> 00:03:50.976
She grabbed Zann and Mellis and dragged them toward the door.

67
00:03:51.956 --> 00:03:54.457
Once they were outside, Zann turned to face her.

68
00:03:54.477 --> 00:03:56.897
"What was that all about?"

69
00:03:57.258 --> 00:03:57.718
he asked.

70
00:03:58.418 --> 00:04:00.238
"I thought you were going to tell Zira off.

71
00:04:00.779 --> 00:04:01.779
Instead you ran away!

72
00:04:01.799 --> 00:04:03.479
That's not like you."

73
00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:04.400
"I know."

74
00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.580
Perda slumped onto a bench.

75
00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.841
"But I was too startled to stay.

76
00:04:09.521 --> 00:04:11.522
Zira sent me a mental message!"

77
00:04:12.122 --> 00:04:13.522
Zann was startled now too.

78
00:04:13.542 --> 00:04:15.803
"But that's really advanced magic!

79
00:04:16.163 --> 00:04:17.864
We haven't even studied it in school yet."

80
00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:18.984
"I know.

81
00:04:19.668 --> 00:04:21.849
I don't know how she did it, but she did."

82
00:04:22.529 --> 00:04:23.470
Perda bit her lip.

83
00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:30.533
"She said that if we tell anyone the truth, she'll send a pack of hungry gorzogs after Mellis!"

84
00:04:30.553 --> 00:04:34.195
"What?" Mellis cried, looking horrified.

85
00:04:34.215 --> 00:04:35.775
"Don't worry.

86
00:04:35.836 --> 00:04:37.176
We won't let her do that."

87
00:04:37.776 --> 00:04:39.957
Perda glanced at Zann, looking troubled.

88
00:04:39.977 --> 00:04:45.160
"Normally, mental messages can only be done at very close range.

89
00:04:45.948 --> 00:04:50.532
I wasn't standing that close to Zira, and I wasn't looking directly at her either.

90
00:04:51.232 --> 00:04:54.735
So how was she able to send that message into my mind?"

91
00:04:55.555 --> 00:04:56.656
Zann thought about that.

92
00:04:57.377 --> 00:05:02.781
His grandfather, Boz, could send mental messages from a distance to his Magic Master friends.

93
00:05:03.622 --> 00:05:07.344
But most ordinary Magicians didn't bother with the difficult spell at all.

94
00:05:08.005 --> 00:05:11.728
It was much easier to use message moths or other methods to communicate.

95
00:05:13.088 --> 00:05:16.949
"Zira is catching on to magic so fast that it's scary," he said.

96
00:05:16.969 --> 00:05:19.610
"Do you think she'd really try to hurt Mellis?"

97
00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.030
"I don't know."

98
00:05:21.911 --> 00:05:24.251
Perda stood and grabbed Mellis by the hand.

99
00:05:24.271 --> 00:05:25.992
"But don't worry, Mellis.

100
00:05:26.532 --> 00:05:30.233
Zann and I won't leave Terrica until we're sure you're safe."

101
00:05:30.253 --> 00:05:34.514
"Th-thanks." Mellis still looked nervous.

102
00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:40.156
"And we'll figure out a way to make sure those two are going to share magic with everyone

103
00:05:40.216 --> 00:05:41.436
too," Perda said.

104
00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.342
"Do we really need to get involved in that?"

105
00:05:44.742 --> 00:05:45.362
Zann asked.

106
00:05:45.382 --> 00:05:48.284
"Like you said, people will figure it out on their own."

107
00:05:49.005 --> 00:05:49.765
Mellis nodded.

108
00:05:49.785 --> 00:05:50.846
"You're right.

109
00:05:51.266 --> 00:05:53.668
And your families must be terribly worried about you.

110
00:05:54.328 --> 00:05:55.229
You should go home.

111
00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:59.192
Zira will have no reason to hurt me if I go along with their plan."

112
00:05:59.212 --> 00:06:01.453
"But their plan isn't right!"

113
00:06:01.874 --> 00:06:02.714
Perda exclaimed.

114
00:06:02.734 --> 00:06:04.235
"I know."

115
00:06:05.136 --> 00:06:05.997
Mellis shrugged.

116
00:06:06.017 --> 00:06:08.038
"But I doubt it will last long.

117
00:06:08.638 --> 00:06:14.065
My uncle can be shallow and greedy—and cowardly—but he's not evil.

118
00:06:14.826 --> 00:06:17.587
Besides, he's terrible at keeping a secret."

119
00:06:18.247 --> 00:06:18.787
She chuckled.

120
00:06:18.807 --> 00:06:23.869
"He'll probably accidentally tell people about magic before long.

121
00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:28.431
What's the harm in letting him and Zira play magic rulers until then?"

122
00:06:29.392 --> 00:06:31.313
Zann thought Mellis had a good point.

123
00:06:32.013 --> 00:06:33.313
But Perda shook her head.

124
00:06:33.333 --> 00:06:39.196
"You may be right about your uncle, but I don't trust Zira one bit," she said.

125
00:06:40.322 --> 00:06:41.191
"We're staying."
